4. Cryptographic, Identity & Regulatory Standards Implemented
================================================================================
- IETF RFC 9162 — Certificate Transparency Version 2.0 (Salted Merkle Tree
  domain separation: 0x00 leaf prefix, 0x01 interior node prefix, Signed Tree Heads).
- IETF RFC 9285 — The Base45 Data Encoding (Alphanumeric QR mode payload encoding).
- IETF RFC 8949 — Concise Binary Object Representation (CBOR).
- IETF RFC 9901 — Selective Disclosure for JWTs (SD-JWT `vc+sd-jwt`, `_sd_alg: sha-256`).
- IETF RFC 7636 — Proof Key for Code Exchange by OAuth Public Clients (PKCE S256).
- W3C Verifiable Credentials Data Model v2.0 & Data Integrity EdDSA Cryptosuites
  (`eddsa-rdfc-2022`).
- C2PA 2.1 — Coalition for Content Provenance and Authenticity (ECDSA P-256
  signed governance manifests).
- Split Conformal Risk Control — Angelopoulos, Bates, Fisch, Lei, Schuster (2022/2024),
  "Conformal Risk Control", ICLR.
- Indian Regulatory & Statutory Frameworks modeled in Declarative YAML Canons:
  - Digital Personal Data Protection (DPDP) Act 2023 (Sections 6, 8, 9) &
    Draft DPDP Rules 2025 (Rule 10 Verifiable Parental Consent).
  - National Assessment and Accreditation Council (NAAC) SSR & DVV Manual.
  - Central Board of Secondary Education (CBSE) Affiliation Bye-Laws 2018
    (Chapter 4 Clauses 4.1–4.8 & Mandatory Public Disclosure Appendix IX).
  - UDISE+ 2024-25 Ministry of Education School Infrastructure Macro Priors.
